WEBVTT

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.000
[This is a fictional story. All characters and events bear no relation to reality]

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.000
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.033
[under the guardian and expert supervision per guidelines]

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:40.033
[Episode 3]

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:42.826
- Hello, sir. - Yeah.

00:00:54.196 --> 00:00:56.148
You're going to stare a hole through it.

00:00:56.148 --> 00:00:58.164
I won't test you, so take it easy.

00:00:58.164 --> 00:01:00.757
It's going to be a long haul, so brace yourself.

00:01:00.757 --> 00:01:02.364
Sir, this...

00:01:02.364 --> 00:01:04.616
What, what is it?

00:01:07.008 --> 00:01:08.583
[Incident Report] Oh, that case.

00:01:08.583 --> 00:01:09.784
The case where a dad was murdered on Christmas night,

00:01:09.784 --> 00:01:11.249
Right in front of his daughter.

00:01:11.249 --> 00:01:12.949
"He abused his wife and child,

00:01:12.949 --> 00:01:15.384
And eventually stabbed his wife to death with a soju bottle."

00:01:15.384 --> 00:01:19.721
"Then, seven years after his release, he tried to kill his daughter?"

00:01:19.721 --> 00:01:21.985
The part about the daughter was never made public.

00:01:21.985 --> 00:01:24.580
She was still a minor at the time,

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.240
And she may have been a witness.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:29.383
A witness?

00:01:29.383 --> 00:01:30.984
She saw Kingfisher?

00:01:30.984 --> 00:01:35.216
If she had, do you think we'd still have zero leads?

00:01:36.816 --> 00:01:38.564
Well, you never know.

00:01:38.564 --> 00:01:42.690
Maybe she really didn't see anything, or maybe she's keeping quiet.

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:46.616
Oh, the daughter's name was 'Oh' something.

00:01:57.995 --> 00:01:59.416
Are you crazy?

00:01:59.416 --> 00:02:01.216
What are you...

00:02:01.868 --> 00:02:04.700
So you really don't want me to die, do you?

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:09.283
The only witness to one of Kingfisher's shootings.

00:02:09.283 --> 00:02:12.449
The only child I ever revealed myself to.

00:02:14.436 --> 00:02:16.983
It's been a while, Oh Seung Ah.

00:02:31.432 --> 00:02:34.168
Merry Christmas, Yoo Bo Na!

00:02:34.168 --> 00:02:35.292
Where's my present?

00:02:35.292 --> 00:02:38.464
Santa Claus will bring you one.

00:02:38.464 --> 00:02:39.824
Yeah, right. Like he'd ever do that.

00:02:39.824 --> 00:02:40.824
You never know.

00:02:40.824 --> 00:02:43.268
He's said to have a very clear sense of right and wrong.

00:02:43.268 --> 00:02:44.920
I don't think he's got a present for you either.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.108
You're a terrible boss for making me work on a day like this.

00:02:47.108 --> 00:02:48.983
It's not like you've got plans.

00:02:48.983 --> 00:02:51.624
Do you have friends? A partner? Family?

00:02:51.624 --> 00:02:54.152
Yet here you are, all by yourself.

00:02:54.152 --> 00:02:57.760
But it's all romance comics, huh?

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.048
Seeing someone these days?

00:02:59.048 --> 00:03:01.652
Go home early. Kids are waiting.

00:03:01.652 --> 00:03:03.864
Will a punk who's meant to die not die just because you delay it a few days?

00:03:03.864 --> 00:03:08.049
He might kill someone first.

00:03:13.892 --> 00:03:16.183
But isn't it possible he's changed?

00:03:16.183 --> 00:03:17.583
Still, he's her dad.

00:03:17.583 --> 00:03:22.583
I know, questioning one more time and never giving up hope until the end.

00:03:22.583 --> 00:03:24.824
That's how you do things.

00:03:24.824 --> 00:03:27.248
If you want to watch a little longer, do it.

00:03:27.248 --> 00:03:31.216
Just don't miss your chance.

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:35.924
It's cold. Take some hand warmers.

00:03:35.924 --> 00:03:38.083
I'm off.

00:03:41.742 --> 00:03:43.974
[Oh Seung Ah's Daily Route]

00:04:04.247 --> 00:04:07.444
<i>I thought, "That day would be the last day of my life."</i>

00:04:07.444 --> 00:04:11.949
<i>"It would be my last Christmas."</i>

00:04:13.464 --> 00:04:16.349
<i>I thought I'd never see this again.</i>

00:04:17.084 --> 00:04:21.248
<i>Whether I died or killed him.</i>

00:04:22.736 --> 00:04:26.352
<i>Right, that's probably why.</i>

00:04:26.352 --> 00:04:28.316
<i>I heard your heart.</i>

00:04:36.212 --> 00:04:38.849
Do you want a Christmas present?

00:04:42.252 --> 00:04:44.699
Then no crying.

00:04:44.699 --> 00:04:46.883
You have to be good.

00:04:47.652 --> 00:04:51.716
I heard that Santa is very clear about right and wrong.

00:04:51.716 --> 00:04:53.272
Miss, who are you?

00:04:53.272 --> 00:04:57.649
Leave the living room window slightly open when you get home.

00:05:03.864 --> 00:05:05.583
See you again.

00:05:08.212 --> 00:05:11.320
<i>Assistant Manager Yoo Bo Na, what on earth are you doing?</i>

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:14.116
<i>Why would you reveal your face like that?</i>

00:05:21.984 --> 00:05:24.183
Does she think she's Santa or something?

00:05:24.828 --> 00:05:27.916
She doesn't even know what I wished for.

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:48.403
<i>I prayed to just let me die quickly instead.</i>

00:05:48.403 --> 00:05:52.883
<i>If God existed, I begged Him to save me from hell.</i>

00:05:52.883 --> 00:05:54.949
<i>Right at that moment...</i>

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:06.749
<i>God really appeared.</i>

00:06:20.248 --> 00:06:22.183
<i>The reason I came back.</i>

00:06:23.316 --> 00:06:26.649
<i>The reason I do this.</i>

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:30.616
<i>Hoping to save even just one person.</i>

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:35.883
<i>Hoping that because of this work, someone might be safe.</i>

00:06:38.412 --> 00:06:40.183
You knew all along.

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.449
You knew everything from the start, but why...

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:48.249
Because I was disappointed.

00:06:49.216 --> 00:06:54.292
I just wanted that child to be happy

00:06:54.292 --> 00:06:56.880
And live a normal life like everyone else,

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:58.549
But that wasn't how things turned out.

00:06:59.716 --> 00:07:02.483
I didn't like your choice.

00:07:04.616 --> 00:07:06.349
I...

00:07:08.649 --> 00:07:11.649
I wanted to be like you.

00:07:12.549 --> 00:07:16.449
I wanted to stand beside you someday,

00:07:16.449 --> 00:07:20.616
So I've been working myself to death until now with just that one dream.

00:07:24.149 --> 00:07:26.192
You shouldn't have.

00:07:26.192 --> 00:07:28.628
You should've followed your own path.

00:07:28.628 --> 00:07:30.949
A safe, bright one.

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:40.516
You told me we'd meet again.

00:07:42.384 --> 00:07:44.108
What?

00:07:47.689 --> 00:07:49.164
See you again.

00:07:49.164 --> 00:07:52.649
No, I just meant I hoped you'd stay safe...

00:07:52.649 --> 00:07:56.372
I don't know about that, but anyway, take responsibility.

00:07:56.372 --> 00:07:57.824
Me?

00:07:57.824 --> 00:08:00.049
You're still such a kid, huh?

00:08:01.672 --> 00:08:03.449
What are you?

00:08:05.592 --> 00:08:08.383
It was the gift I had desperately wished for.

00:08:09.168 --> 00:08:11.484
<i>You were my Santa,</i>

00:08:11.484 --> 00:08:13.616
The savior of my life.

00:08:16.249 --> 00:08:18.476
So take responsibility.

00:08:18.476 --> 00:08:21.920
And yet you drugged my husband?

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:24.724
It wasn't poison. Just a sleeping pill.

00:08:24.724 --> 00:08:27.049
Would Kingfisher fall for something like that?

00:08:27.049 --> 00:08:29.916
I know it was a sleeping pill, okay?

00:08:29.916 --> 00:08:31.816
Then why bring a gun?

00:08:31.816 --> 00:08:33.704
The bullets were real too.

00:08:33.704 --> 00:08:35.520
You actually fired it!

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:39.649
Because you messed with someone you never should have.

00:08:45.048 --> 00:08:47.349
What an idiot...

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:03.883
You've really been working hard, huh?

00:09:05.724 --> 00:09:07.816
So it was from this point on?

00:09:13.788 --> 00:09:16.816
You didn't like my choice either?

00:09:16.816 --> 00:09:18.216
About six years ago...

00:09:18.216 --> 00:09:21.516
[Six Years Ago]

00:09:25.164 --> 00:09:26.416
<i>I saw you by chance.</i>

00:09:26.416 --> 00:09:27.944
Honey!

00:09:27.944 --> 00:09:30.383
<i>I recognized you instantly.</i>

00:09:31.056 --> 00:09:34.016
<i>Because I never forgot you for a single day after that.</i>

00:09:41.376 --> 00:09:45.128
<i>It felt like there was a hole in my chest.</i>

00:09:45.128 --> 00:09:47.764
<i>The woman who'd been my god and heroine</i>

00:09:47.764 --> 00:09:51.256
<i>had become just an ordinary, fragile person.</i>

00:09:51.256 --> 00:09:53.383
So you're more like an anti-fan.

00:09:55.783 --> 00:09:58.068
So?

00:09:58.068 --> 00:09:59.648
I want to bring you back.

00:09:59.648 --> 00:10:02.816
Back to the old Kingfisher, the woman I used to know.

00:10:04.116 --> 00:10:05.632
So you're an idiot after all.

00:10:05.632 --> 00:10:07.320
I think I told you.

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:10.752
You made your choice, and I respected it.

00:10:10.752 --> 00:10:13.700
Even if I didn't like it, it was your life.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:15.404
I only did what I had to do.

00:10:15.404 --> 00:10:18.349
How you live with it afterward is up to you.

00:10:18.349 --> 00:10:20.649
But Kingfisher...

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:24.556
You seem to be mistaken about something.

00:10:24.556 --> 00:10:27.249
If I were your savior,

00:10:27.249 --> 00:10:30.416
The man who saved Kingfisher was Kwon Tae Seong.

00:10:31.472 --> 00:10:33.212
It was him.

00:10:34.992 --> 00:10:36.783
That guy...

00:10:37.648 --> 00:10:40.564
Saved your life?

00:10:40.564 --> 00:10:42.483
He saved something even greater.

00:10:45.076 --> 00:10:47.449
I received an even greater gift.

00:11:08.196 --> 00:11:10.816
It's Yoo Bo Na!

00:11:11.644 --> 00:11:14.000
Honey, do you know where we are now?

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:16.183
A cafe...

00:11:18.449 --> 00:11:21.478
Never thought I'd get a call telling me to pick up my husband from a cafe

00:11:21.478 --> 00:11:25.252
Because it was closing.

00:11:25.252 --> 00:11:27.632
What is going on?

00:11:27.632 --> 00:11:29.749
Oh, my!

00:11:30.956 --> 00:11:33.783
Did I fall asleep? What? Why?

00:11:35.592 --> 00:11:38.116
But when did I fall asleep?

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:43.620
It's nighttime already!

00:11:47.484 --> 00:11:49.596
Our date...

00:11:49.596 --> 00:11:51.092
Well, it's all over for today.

00:11:51.092 --> 00:11:53.249
What are you going to do about this?

00:11:56.057 --> 00:11:58.340
I'm sorry. I'll...

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:01.849
I'll do the dishes for a month. I'm really sorry.

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:05.849
You think that'll make up for it?

00:12:08.984 --> 00:12:10.456
No?

00:12:10.456 --> 00:12:14.012
I'll also take Yul to daycare every morning for a month.

00:12:14.012 --> 00:12:15.844
I'm really sorry.

00:12:15.844 --> 00:12:17.860
Okay, I'll accept that.

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:23.648
And you'll read Yul a bedtime story every night for a month.

00:12:23.648 --> 00:12:25.360
Okay, okay. Deal.

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:26.628
- Okay? - Yeah.

00:12:26.628 --> 00:12:28.712
- Good. - I'm really sorry.

00:12:28.712 --> 00:12:30.300
I ruined our precious time together.

00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:33.749
Really, I'll really make it up to you. Double, I'll really make it up double.

00:12:36.432 --> 00:12:37.432
What are we going to do about this?

00:12:37.432 --> 00:12:39.683
Honey, I'm so embarrassed. Let's get out of here.

00:12:39.683 --> 00:12:42.783
Se Ah keeps calling. Get up, now.

00:12:44.020 --> 00:12:45.088
Are you okay?

00:12:45.088 --> 00:12:46.993
- I'm okay. - Can you walk?

00:12:46.993 --> 00:12:48.693
Yeah.

00:12:50.612 --> 00:12:55.916
If what I fed him was really poison, I'd have died by your hand, right?

00:12:56.720 --> 00:12:58.420
Director.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:02.649
If you get caught calling me like that at work too, seriously...

00:13:03.428 --> 00:13:05.349
You're really going to die, okay?

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:09.872
At work too...

00:13:09.872 --> 00:13:12.983
At work too...

00:13:14.983 --> 00:13:17.349
See you at work?

00:13:40.749 --> 00:13:45.183
<i>Is family really worth risking your life for?</i>

00:13:45.183 --> 00:13:48.049
- Heave-ho! - Wow!

00:13:48.884 --> 00:13:50.583
Mom, I'm hungry.

00:13:50.583 --> 00:13:52.012
Yul, are you hungry?

00:13:52.012 --> 00:13:53.848
It's time for Yul to eat, isn't it?

00:13:53.848 --> 00:13:55.740
Since we're already out, should we eat out before going home?

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:57.696
Honey, your mom's radish kimchi is perfectly fermented.

00:13:57.696 --> 00:13:59.644
It's because I thought you might be tired.

00:13:59.644 --> 00:14:00.849
You said that because you were worried I'd be tired?

00:14:00.849 --> 00:14:02.527
Yeah.

00:14:02.527 --> 00:14:04.680
Honey, look at the flowers. Aren't they pretty?

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:06.016
- You're prettier. - Really?

00:14:06.016 --> 00:14:08.360
- Yeah. - Is Mommy prettier than flowers?

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:10.583
- Yeah! - Really?

00:14:11.408 --> 00:14:13.483
<i>That was the wrong question.</i>

00:14:14.284 --> 00:14:16.520
<i>It's not about risking my life.</i>

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:19.549
<i>My family is my life.</i>

00:14:28.544 --> 00:14:31.720
So in the end, he saved one person.

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:35.279
That girl would have died if it weren't for Kingfisher, right?

00:14:35.279 --> 00:14:38.349
So, the conclusion is...

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:41.576
Man, that's just incredible!

00:14:41.576 --> 00:14:44.649
That's why he has over a million fans!

00:14:45.448 --> 00:14:47.572
Hey, aren't you going to snap out of it?

00:14:47.572 --> 00:14:49.483
Is that something a detective should say?

00:14:50.472 --> 00:14:52.172
I'm sorry, sir!

00:14:52.849 --> 00:14:57.449
Hey, all the victims killed by Kingfisher were criminals.

00:14:57.449 --> 00:15:00.716
But does that justify murder?

00:15:00.716 --> 00:15:03.408
- No, it doesn't. - The law is a social contract.

00:15:03.408 --> 00:15:04.672
Does he have the right

00:15:04.672 --> 00:15:08.098
To break that contract and personally judge someone?

00:15:08.098 --> 00:15:09.249
- No, he doesn't! - Should we,

00:15:09.249 --> 00:15:11.373
As police officers, catch someone like that or not?

00:15:11.373 --> 00:15:13.816
- We should. - How?

00:15:16.224 --> 00:15:18.312
Well?

00:15:18.312 --> 00:15:21.283
That's the conclusion. Got it?

00:15:24.756 --> 00:15:27.449
Let's get it together! Get it together!

00:15:28.936 --> 00:15:30.316
Here.

00:15:30.316 --> 00:15:32.172
Thank you.

00:15:32.172 --> 00:15:33.516
Dig through the files all the way.

00:15:33.516 --> 00:15:35.416
Up to the final case four years ago.

00:15:35.416 --> 00:15:39.183
You'll see another side of Kingfisher.

00:15:53.808 --> 00:15:56.983
Hey, don't go too deep.

00:15:56.983 --> 00:15:58.483
You might run into snakes.

00:15:58.483 --> 00:16:02.649
You have to dig deep to find anything.

00:16:03.908 --> 00:16:10.683
The good ones are always the ones that stay hidden.

00:16:18.964 --> 00:16:20.784
What? What's that?

00:16:20.784 --> 00:16:23.249
- Is that a snake? - Over there...

00:16:23.249 --> 00:16:25.349
Oh, my...

00:16:27.583 --> 00:16:29.816
[Not Today]

00:16:29.816 --> 00:16:32.449
[Social Affairs Desk]

00:16:33.304 --> 00:16:35.516
[Caller ID Restricted: I'd like to provide a tip about Kingfisher]

00:16:36.352 --> 00:16:39.383
Well, did anyone come by while I was asleep?

00:16:39.383 --> 00:16:41.808
Someone who came while you were sleeping?

00:16:41.808 --> 00:16:43.004
Yeah.

00:16:43.004 --> 00:16:46.583
Well, I don't think I saw anyone.

00:16:48.438 --> 00:16:50.105
A tip about Kingfisher?

00:16:50.105 --> 00:16:51.503
You scared me!

00:16:51.503 --> 00:16:53.488
Jeez, stop popping up from behind me like that.

00:16:53.488 --> 00:16:56.369
My colleague Kwon Tae Seong!

00:16:56.369 --> 00:16:57.560
Jeez...

00:16:57.560 --> 00:16:59.149
So you finally latched onto the Kingfisher case, huh?

00:16:59.149 --> 00:17:00.383
I knew it.

00:17:00.383 --> 00:17:03.183
A swallow can't just pass by a mill, right?

00:17:05.752 --> 00:17:07.928
It's a sparrow, not a swallow.

00:17:07.928 --> 00:17:11.448
I was going to take it and pass it to the right person if it was worth pursuing.

00:17:11.448 --> 00:17:12.583
What is it?

00:17:12.583 --> 00:17:14.144
What is it? What is it?

00:17:14.144 --> 00:17:16.114
Is it huge? A scoop?

00:17:16.114 --> 00:17:18.683
Did that person really not come?

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:22.149
Or did they come but fail to meet?

00:17:22.783 --> 00:17:24.716
There's been no contact since then.

00:17:24.716 --> 00:17:26.930
Was it just a prank?

00:17:26.930 --> 00:17:28.716
What are you talking about?

00:17:30.616 --> 00:17:35.216
But why does my colleague and economics reporter, Go Ji Soon,

00:17:36.044 --> 00:17:39.549
Always slack off instead of doing his job?

00:17:41.524 --> 00:17:44.512
You got stood up, huh? You got stood up.

00:17:44.512 --> 00:17:48.036
Man, how can you talk about being stood up by a source

00:17:48.036 --> 00:17:50.549
And make it sound like an editor-in-chief's report?

00:17:51.284 --> 00:17:53.238
Get out of here, you punk!

00:17:53.238 --> 00:17:54.812
Keep your chin up, okay?

00:17:54.812 --> 00:17:56.512
Fighting!

00:17:58.576 --> 00:18:01.448
Hello! Good morning!

00:18:01.448 --> 00:18:02.496
Hello.

00:18:02.496 --> 00:18:04.392
- Good morning. - She's so cheerful, isn't she?

00:18:04.392 --> 00:18:05.624
- Hello! - Good morning.

00:18:05.624 --> 00:18:08.346
She has no idea what kind of person her senior is,

00:18:08.346 --> 00:18:10.549
And she's still that cheerful.

00:18:14.156 --> 00:18:18.412
- Hi. - Good day. Hello.

00:18:18.412 --> 00:18:19.444
Mr. Tae Seong!

00:18:19.444 --> 00:18:23.266
I didn't know what you liked, so I brought one of everything.

00:18:23.266 --> 00:18:25.475
Have whichever one you feel like.

00:18:25.475 --> 00:18:28.016
I'll take this one. Thank you, Ms. Hae Na.

00:18:29.008 --> 00:18:32.149
I already have my usual drink, so I'm fine.

00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:37.479
That's not good...

00:18:37.479 --> 00:18:38.883
I'll enjoy it then, Ms. Hae Na.

00:18:38.883 --> 00:18:41.120
Wow, Mr. Kwon is so lucky.

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:42.184
Thank you, Ms. Hae Na.

00:18:42.184 --> 00:18:43.184
Ms. Hae Na, thank you.

00:18:43.184 --> 00:18:45.549
There's no one like you, Ms. Hae Na.

00:18:57.929 --> 00:18:59.629
Ms. Gu Hae Na.

00:19:00.895 --> 00:19:02.452
- Yes! - Here...

00:19:02.452 --> 00:19:05.352
I organized some potential stories we could look into.

00:19:05.352 --> 00:19:08.256
